WEBVTT

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:10.310
Rear Admiral Spaurh Aronn Saicspath Nimh Laitpanr Painaich commands the Futuune patrol fleet.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:19.110
She is a member of the Spaurh family which pride themselves on being close kin to Lafiel's Ablïarsec Imperial Family.

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:24.370
The Spoor family consists of over 500 titled members.

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:29.750
Moreover, the Duchess's clan is seen as the heir to the Spoors.

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:33.920
That is not all. With its three inhabited planets...

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:40.220
...the Letopanyu Duchy is known for its abundant nature which they openly share with others.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:48.480
This Duchess controls the richest domain in terms of wealth and tradition with the exception of the Ablïarsec.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:56.690
If she chose, she could have left the Laburec to enjoy a lifestyle befitting a royal heir.

00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:58.990
However...

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.710
I'm bored.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:20.220
I always dreamed of becoming captain and fighting an enemy...

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:23.140
...but while I was captain, there was no war...

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.720
...and now that there's a war, I just have these boring tasks.

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:30.100
Am I unlucky or what?

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:33.310
Flagship

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:33.310
Keildij

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:36.530
Beautiful, Rear Admiral Spoor!

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:42.320
Deploy as many mines here as possible!

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:45.870
We cannot allow it to close again!

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:48.000
We cannot lose to Futuune!

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:22.330
Logh Labyrena

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:22.330
Lady of Chaos

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.480
Enemy space-time bubble!

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:32.480
Intercepting our path at bearing 010, distance 30 units.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.650
Quantity, about 300!

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:36.320
Looks like the enemy's main force!

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:39.280
They've deployed reinforcements against us.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:40.530
We must take action to evade them!

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:42.080
Please.

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:44.490
Stop making such a fuss on my serene bridge.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:51.130
Make the calculations. Do we have time?

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:52.920
Uh, right away!

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:56.920
Maintain present route.

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:21.950
We should see the enemy's front line fleet any time now.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:24.700
The enemy's line of battle...

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:27.790
...is completely focused on stopping Futuune.

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:29.830
There's hardly any threat to the main fleet.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:31.330
All right!

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:33.130
All vessels, prepare to advance.

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:36.090
Rokeil, annihilate the front line vessels to the right.

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:37.960
Wakapeil, wipe out the vessels to the left.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:40.090
Byuuldef and Kitiil, follow me.

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:44.100
Unless we start getting aggressive...

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:45.970
...Futuune will walk off with the best stuff!

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:51.810
Too slow.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:55.570
We'll send half our fleet at once to destroy those ships.

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:57.530
Executive officer!

00:04:58.240 --> 00:04:58.650
Yes!

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:02.110
I detest the little jobs.

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:04.950
You tell each unit what their respective targets are.

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:05.870
Right.

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:08.660
Oh, and tell them they don't need to leave any for us.

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.670
Are we going to standby on reserve?

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:13.710
No.

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:15.790
I want the ones right there!

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:19.170
They look like...

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:22.590
...oversized transport ships of some sort.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:23.890
Shouldn't we just ignore them?

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:27.560
They could be reinforcement battleships disguised as such.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:31.690
They might try to sneak through and hit us at the very end.

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:34.350
I hate when that happens, so we'll get them first.

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:35.650
Right.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:40.280
All units have acknowledged target orders.

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:41.530
Very well.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:44.320
All units, spread out!

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:47.660
The main event Fire Dance is just about to begin.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:50.950
We are Futuune, the Goddess of Dance.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:53.620
Show them what great dancers we are!

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:58.040
<i>Inspector. We've sighted</i> <i>two suspicious people.</i>

00:05:58.630 --> 00:05:59.630
Where are they?

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:01.210
<i>At the Limzairh Inn...</i>

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:02.590
<i>...but they're no longer here.</i>

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:04.220
So they got away from you.

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:06.510
<i>No, they were gone</i> <i>by the time we arrived.</i>

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:08.260
What makes you think they were suspicious?

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:11.730
<i>Neither left the room</i> <i>even once during their stay.</i>

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:12.230
Witnesses?

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:15.900
<i>The girl had black</i> <i>hair and eyes...</i>

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:17.610
<i>...and creamy skin.</i>

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.400
<i>She was apparently</i> <i>very beautiful.</i>

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:22.320
"Very", he says.

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:28.530
You think we're just a bunch of idealists, don't you?

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:32.250
That there's no way the Empire will recognize independence...

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:35.710
...just because we have her as our hostage.

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:37.500
Well, you knew that?

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:40.590
What we're after is a spaceship.

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:42.210
Not independence?

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:44.470
For our independence.

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:47.840
Min wants to gain independence right away...

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:51.310
...but I believe we should approach it in steps.

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:55.890
If you want to get on a spaceship, why not just become citizens?

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:58.360
Our objective is not to ride spaceships.

00:06:58.360 --> 00:06:59.610
We want to own one...

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:01.820
...a spaceship that'll make us free!

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:04.240
That's impossible.

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:07.700
All interstellar Imperial ships belong to the Empress.

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:10.780
Not even the top nobility own their personal interstellar ships.

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:16.040
But we see numerous ships of companies and feudal lords coming in and out of the spaceport.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.540
Those are all leased out.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:21.090
The Imperial merchant group leases them out, crew included.

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:24.380
The lessee has control over the vessel size and contract term...

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:27.220
...but the merchant group has control over the crew.

00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:29.970
Then what's going to become of our dream?

00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:40.400
So, what are you going to do? That's our destination, right?

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:42.570
That was our destination.

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:44.480
That's my villa.

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:46.990
We were going to use it to confine you...

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:48.990
...but I'm no longer sure you're worth it.

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:52.950
Think about it carefully.

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:55.830
Why are Abhs so arrogant?

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:58.000
Don't let it bother you.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:59.880
You'll stress yourself out.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:02.460
I was only trying to be helpful!

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:04.380
Look over there!

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:07.090
Min, is that one of yours?

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:08.050
No.

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:13.470
The United Mankind.

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:25.030
Who are you people? Citizens?

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:27.110
I ask you the same question!

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:33.870
I'm Lieutenant Commander Alanga of the United Mankind Peace Force, Sfagnomr division...

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:36.040
...RC district military police.

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:38.620
I'm the owner of that villa.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:42.210
My friends and I were on our way to my place for a party.

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:46.210
Then you must be Min Kulsup, a member of the Independence Party.

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:49.090
Former member. I left the party three years ago.

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:51.010
But you are Min, aren't you?

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:51.760
That's right!

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:53.510
You're under arrest.

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:55.930
What? For what?

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:59.270
A large quantity of weapons was found in your villa.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:03.690
There is a real risk that your Independence Party is a cover organization...

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:10.450
...susceptible to reactionary and revolutionary actions in support of the Empire.

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:15.990
There's no point in resisting arrest.

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:18.200
They've completely misunderstood us.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:21.960
Don't do it!

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:32.680
What are you...?!

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:33.720
Run!

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:38.850
Damn!

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:40.100
That way!

00:09:48.530 --> 00:09:50.070
Commander! Commander!

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:51.110
Hurry!

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:56.320
Damn Abhs! Now, I've become a fugitive!

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:57.580
Be quiet.

00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:59.040
I'll listen to your complaints later!

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:01.330
This way!

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:07.840
Look!

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:16.300
You just had to come, didn't you?

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:25.770
This way!

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:32.990
Get in!

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:36.070
Hurry!

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:44.830
Outta my way!

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:55.430
Is everyone here?

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:56.510
Looks that way.

00:10:57.140 --> 00:10:58.220
Okay, this way.

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:01.430
Oh, before that...

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:12.190
Where are we?

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:13.610
It's a lava cave.

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:15.860
Then, what's the hole we just came through?

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:19.660
That's an escape route I made just in case.

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:22.330
You know, you guys have really made things difficult for us!

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:25.250
Now, they know my name.

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:28.540
And as an enemy collaborator, no less!

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:29.880
I apologize.

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:33.510
There's no excuse for involving you in this.

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:36.880
However, we can't afford to get caught ourselves.

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:39.470
Long ago...

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:43.470
...there was a guy who jumped into a thorn bush.

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:45.560
What are you talking about?

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:51.770
Can you hear it?

00:11:55.490 --> 00:11:56.190
They're coming.

00:11:56.990 --> 00:11:58.240
Jinto, turn out the light.

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:04.580
Naturally, the guy was covered in scratches.

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:05.750
Who was?

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:08.040
The guy that jumped into the thorn bush.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:10.170
I went to the hospital to see him...

00:12:10.170 --> 00:12:12.920
...and asked him why he did such a thing.

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:14.500
The guy replied...

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:18.680
...it seemed like a good idea at the time.

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:24.720
This path will take us to the main tunnel.

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:27.600
Once we reach the tunnel, there are several holes leading out.

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:30.400
You must go ahead of me.

00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:31.310
What do you mean?!

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:35.570
I can't afford to cause you any more trouble.

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:37.650
I'll stop them here.

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:38.570
Go on.

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:42.990
I've never heard of kidnappers being saved by their hostages.

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:45.370
Let's go.

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:47.370
Nothing's going to change this girl's mind.

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:49.080
Get going.

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:49.830
The enemy's near.

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:51.210
All right.

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:55.500
If you get out alive, let's meet again.

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:56.920
So long, girl.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:07.100
You're not thinking of getting rid of me, too, are you?

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:10.730
Of course not. You're not much of a marksman...

00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:12.100
...but having you is better than nothing.

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:22.700
I hope they don't use a cannon in here.

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:24.320
We'd be buried alive.

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:25.830
Don't worry.

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:29.000
Kin of the stars aren't meant to die in soil.

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:35.840
I see they got here first.

00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:37.130
What do you think?

00:13:37.130 --> 00:13:38.960
Should we go underground after them too?

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:42.630
Leave the underground chase to the army.

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:44.640
But, Inspector...

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:49.220
We call the guys of Guzonyu local police "moles".

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:53.060
We can get detailed information on this lava cave.

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:53.600
You mean...

00:13:54.690 --> 00:13:56.860
We can wait for them at the other end.

00:13:59.150 --> 00:13:59.740
Run!

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:07.280
We'll wait for them here.

00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:09.040
Right.

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:12.410
Jinto, take a firing stance with one knee on the ground.

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:12.910
Okay.

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:17.630
When I give you the sign, fire away, up and down.

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:20.510
But, I'm uneasy about shooting at an enemy I can't see.

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:22.920
It wouldn't make a difference if you did see them.

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:24.510
Thanks for your fair assessment.

00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:24.970
Now!

00:14:31.810 --> 00:14:32.270
Jinto!

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:36.480
Keep going!

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:44.950
Hurry!

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:50.990
Space-time bubble 661, space-time separation!

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:52.450
Here they come.

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:55.420
Six space-time bubbles for attack ships detected.

00:14:55.420 --> 00:14:57.420
Course, 345. Distance, 16 units.

00:14:58.040 --> 00:14:59.250
You sure?

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:00.340
They're not mines?

00:15:00.340 --> 00:15:01.380
Correct.

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:04.340
Weapons officer, how many mines do we have left?

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:05.970
Four on this ship...

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:07.840
...four on Bogbyursh...

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:09.510
...and five on Hasunbyursh...

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:10.810
...for a total of thirteen.

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:13.850
I can do addition, you know.

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:17.150
Front line vessels, commence mine battle.

00:15:17.150 --> 00:15:18.560
Crush them.

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:29.950
Executive officer.

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:30.830
What is it, ma'am?

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:33.580
What do you think is the worst crime an officer can commit?

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:37.420
Insubordination against one's superior?

00:15:37.420 --> 00:15:39.960
No. It's to be a fool.

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:42.380
What kind of fool sends only six attack vessels...

00:15:42.380 --> 00:15:44.760
...to get rid of three patrol ships?

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:45.720
I see.

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:48.930
I may not take my job seriously, but I am no fool.

00:15:48.930 --> 00:15:51.600
I will never needlessly sacrifice the lives of my subordinates.

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:52.470
Right.

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:55.270
I can also do without fools on my staff.

00:15:55.270 --> 00:15:56.940
I, Duchess Laitpanr...

00:15:56.940 --> 00:15:58.730
...decide who I play with.

00:15:59.150 --> 00:16:01.650
But never who I'll play against.

00:16:04.070 --> 00:16:06.400
I'll do my best to be a worthy playmate!

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:10.910
I have high hopes for you.

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:13.080
One minute to space-time convergence!

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:17.660
No sign of surrender from 661 as of yet.

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:18.920
As I expected.

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:20.170
Senior navigator!

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:22.960
Make it so that the three ships enter space-time together!

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:24.130
Aye-aye!

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.300
Notify all units.

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:29.680
Fire electromagnetic guns upon space-time convergence!

00:16:32.850 --> 00:16:36.020
Now, I wonder what we'll find in there.

00:16:36.020 --> 00:16:37.480
I'm getting excited already.

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:39.350
Ten seconds to space-time convergence!

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:40.900
Here we go!

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:41.810
Five,

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:42.690
four,

00:16:42.690 --> 00:16:43.730
three,

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:44.690
two,

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:45.780
one,

00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:46.940
Space-time convergence!

00:16:47.530 --> 00:16:48.570
They're surrendering!

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:52.030
We've received a surrender signal by radio transmission.

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:53.160
Halt attack!

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:54.120
All units!

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:56.410
We've got to halt the attack!

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:59.500
I'd stain the Spoor name if I fire at surrendered vessels.

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:02.250
Hasunbyursh has fired!

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:03.420
Electromagnetic guns!

00:17:03.670 --> 00:17:04.420
Detonate the mines!

00:17:07.630 --> 00:17:11.010
Goodness... Why couldn't they tell us by inter-bubble transmission?

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:12.930
Did they think they could get away?

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:15.640
So they were transport ships after all.

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:20.980
Even I make mistakes at times.

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:24.110
A transfer shuttle has arrived from Futuune.

00:17:24.110 --> 00:17:25.190
What's the situation?

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:27.730
They've imprisoned a group of civil servants.

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:30.320
What are government officials doing in battle?

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:32.820
It seems the United Mankind has...

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:35.620
...a custom of having civilians present at battles.

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:39.330
Their methods are totally incomprehensible.

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:42.540
Well, in any case, I guess that means we win.

00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:45.500
Yes. It's the obvious conclusion.

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:48.510
It's too easy to be thrilled about, but still worth a celebration.

00:17:48.510 --> 00:17:50.590
Order all fleets to assemble.

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:51.630
Aye-aye.

00:17:52.220 --> 00:17:55.550
Also, there's one more job for Futuune.

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:00.140
Detecting enemy fleet!

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:02.520
Direction, 105, 010...

00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:04.520
...distance, 0.12 light seconds...

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:07.820
...relative speed, 217.5 üethdagh per second.

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:09.320
Fleet consisting of about 20 vessels.

00:18:09.860 --> 00:18:12.360
Type of vessels in enemy fleet confirmed.

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:14.280
They're believed to be 12 large transport ships...

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:18.080
...one patrol ship, and 6 attack ships.

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:21.620
Probability of victory, 98.7%.

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:23.710
Shall we send out a demand for surrender?

00:18:23.710 --> 00:18:24.620
There's no need.

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:26.460
They'll surrender if they want to.

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:28.000
Message from enemy ship.

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:32.550
"We have 22 prisoners, including the Marquis of Sfagnomr."

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:34.550
"Cease fire and allow us to pass."

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:37.050
Communications officer.

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:37.930
Yes, ma'am!

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:39.510
Reply to the enemy ship!

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:41.350
Yes ma'am. And the message?

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:47.810
I am Rear Admiral Spoor, Commander of Futuune patrol.

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:51.070
Be thankful for the generosity shown by the Laburec.

00:18:51.070 --> 00:18:53.570
I allow you the opportunity to surrender.

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:57.740
I will wait until you are within 0.08 light seconds of us.

00:18:57.740 --> 00:19:00.540
Should you miss this opportunity to surrender...

00:19:00.540 --> 00:19:03.330
...we have an even sweeter destiny in line for you.

00:19:04.330 --> 00:19:05.500
More precisely...

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:07.880
...you will have the honor of dying with Abh nobility!

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:10.630
Count your blessings as you disintegrate into the ether!

00:19:12.010 --> 00:19:13.420
Notify all vessels.

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:14.170
Aye-aye.

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:19.350
We will open fire as soon as we're within 0.08 light seconds.

00:19:19.350 --> 00:19:20.850
Once we start firing...

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:24.140
...you can ignore all surrender signals from the enemy.

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:26.310
Shower them with firepower until there's nothing left!

00:19:26.900 --> 00:19:27.730
Please wait one moment!

00:19:28.610 --> 00:19:30.230
What is it, Executive officer?

00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:32.530
Firing at a surrendered enemy...

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:35.030
...will scar the honor of the Empire and Laburec.

00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:39.410
You're right.

00:19:39.410 --> 00:19:41.830
Firing at a surrendered enemy is not a pretty sight.

00:19:41.830 --> 00:19:42.910
Let's not then.

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:46.670
Yes. Thank you for accepting my suggestion.

00:19:46.670 --> 00:19:51.210
By the way, am I free to decide how to transport the prisoners?

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:52.210
Of course.

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:54.210
You are the commander, Your Excellency.

00:19:54.550 --> 00:19:55.590
Very well then.

00:19:55.590 --> 00:19:58.340
How many people do you think the enemy fleet has in total?

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:00.970
Well, they have 12 large transport ships...

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:02.890
...so, I'd guess about 25,000 people?

00:20:02.890 --> 00:20:03.720
I see.

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:06.390
Then we can fit them on one Talse transport ship, can't we?

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:07.060
One ship?!

00:20:07.770 --> 00:20:09.270
Well, it's not impossible...

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:11.230
Then calculate this.

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:14.190
If we board 24,000 prisoners on a Talse transport ship...

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:18.200
...and make passage through normal space to the capital...

00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:20.240
...how long would it take in travel time?

00:20:20.700 --> 00:20:22.490
Through normal space?

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:23.700
That's right.

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:29.620
Approximately 58,300 years.

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:30.580
Really?

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:34.000
I can't imagine the prisoners would be too happy about that.

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:35.340
I wouldn't think so.

00:20:35.340 --> 00:20:37.720
Then let's shorten the travel time for them.

00:20:38.180 --> 00:20:40.970
There won't be any use for space-time generators.

00:20:40.970 --> 00:20:42.720
No need for stabilizers.

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:44.390
And they won't need a crew.

00:20:44.390 --> 00:20:47.100
And remove gravity control devices.

00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:48.770
It still seems quite heavy.

00:20:48.770 --> 00:20:51.690
Did you include food and water in your calculations?

00:20:51.690 --> 00:20:53.690
I've included a 1-year-supply...

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:57.150
...and agricultural facilities to supply them with minimum...

00:20:57.150 --> 00:20:59.110
There's no need for agricultural facilities!

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:00.610
Remove those as well.

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:03.700
While we're at it, should we also delete food, water...

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:06.410
...and all air purifiers?

00:21:06.790 --> 00:21:10.830
Don't be stupid. The prisoners would die if we did something like that.

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:13.340
I can't imagine doing anything so cruel.

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:16.590
That should make it a lot lighter than it was.

00:21:16.590 --> 00:21:18.380
Recalculate the travel time.

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:20.340
I don't think it makes that much of a difference.

00:21:21.470 --> 00:21:23.470
About 49,100 years.

00:21:23.890 --> 00:21:25.510
What did I tell you?

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:27.970
We reduced the time by almost 10,000 years.

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:29.430
But still...

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:34.360
Communications officer, notify all units.

00:21:34.360 --> 00:21:37.730
Respect their wishes to surrender at any time.

00:21:37.730 --> 00:21:41.490
However, those surrendering after battle has begun...

00:21:41.490 --> 00:21:45.410
...will travel to the capital through normal space only.

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:51.210
To save travel time, the ship will be stripped of space-time generators, gravity control devices...

00:21:51.210 --> 00:21:54.750
...and stabilizers, and there will be no crew.

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:58.960
Prisoners will be supplied with a year's supply of food and water.

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:02.470
Arrival time is estimated at 49,000 years.

00:22:02.760 --> 00:22:03.550
That's all.

00:22:03.550 --> 00:22:05.220
Please wait, Your Excellency.

00:22:05.220 --> 00:22:07.180
Silence, Executive officer.

00:22:07.180 --> 00:22:10.430
Any further suggestions will be considered insubordination.

00:22:12.770 --> 00:22:14.230
A lady of chaos...

00:22:17.770 --> 00:22:19.940
I like that title.

00:22:22.150 --> 00:22:24.320
Looks like they haven't given up yet.

00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:26.490
On the bright side, they're marking the route back for us.

00:22:28.160 --> 00:22:31.080
When I'm with you, I tend to forget my worries.

00:22:31.080 --> 00:22:32.870
The universe has much hope.

00:22:42.300 --> 00:22:43.260
We have a problem.

00:22:43.630 --> 00:22:44.550
What's wrong?

00:22:45.930 --> 00:22:46.850
They're closing in.

00:22:47.970 --> 00:22:49.100
It's a dead end.

00:22:49.600 --> 00:22:50.350
Jinto, get down!

00:24:30.530 --> 00:24:34.120
I never imagined I'd experience being a corpse while I'm alive.

00:24:34.120 --> 00:24:35.580
Does it still hurt?

00:24:35.910 --> 00:24:37.580
It's just a scratch.

00:24:38.500 --> 00:24:40.040
This is humiliating.

00:24:40.040 --> 00:24:44.670
To have to ride a ship with no spatial sensors or gooheiks.

00:24:44.670 --> 00:24:46.380
This is not a ship.

00:24:46.380 --> 00:24:49.300
It's a coffin. C-O-F-F-I-N.

00:24:49.300 --> 00:24:51.180
It's cramped in here.

00:24:51.180 --> 00:24:54.430
I suddenly have the urge to get away from you. Stay away.

00:24:54.430 --> 00:24:56.680
Ouch! I'm injured,

00:24:56.680 --> 00:24:58.020
be careful.

00:24:57.230 --> 00:25:00.020
Next episode

00:24:57.230 --> 00:25:00.020
Trouble Soaring Through Heaven

00:24:57.230 --> 00:25:00.020
Robïach Saisera

00:24:58.020 --> 00:24:59.390
I thought it was just a scratch.
